- The **traced issue chain** is genuine and consequential: issue #16476 (catalog), PR #16584 and commit 7d9d4fc6 (byte-identical recapture, patch and regression test read in full), release membership now pinned by F1. The §3 design lesson (bounded-sample inference is a hypothesis; pin dialect/schema after full-file validation; never present preview claims as full-dataset properties) is well-founded and should survive into the final proposal unchanged, with the corrected release window.
- The **status-model safety property** (W2): restart/interrupt/failure paths never produce "current" — matches the brief's non-negotiable. The W-verified transitivity requirement (two failed drafts documented in the receipt) is a real modeling insight worth preserving.
